---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro'

const effectiveDate = 'March 18, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security Architecture, Technical Safeguards & SLA"
  description="ShorelineOps Care OS Technical Security Whitepaper, SOC 2 Safeguards, Fail-Closed Database Architecture, and 99.9% Uptime SLA."
  canonicalPath="/security"
>
  <div class="relative py-16 sm:py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/60 border border-purple-200 dark:border-purple-800/80 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 text-xs font-mono font-semibold mb-4">
          <Icon name="server" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
          <span>SECURITY WHITEPAPER & SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENT</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
          Security Architecture & Cloud SLA
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Effective Date: {effectiveDate} · Defense-in-Depth Engineering · Zero Split-Brain High Availability
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Key Metrics Frosted Card -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-xl border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-sm mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-4">Enterprise Reliability Commitments</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-slate-700/60">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-mono">99.9%</div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1">Monthly Uptime SLA</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-slate-700/60">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono">&lt; 1 hr</div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1">Disaster RTO</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-slate-700/60">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 font-mono">&lt; 15 min</div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1">Disaster RPO</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-slate-700/60">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-mono">72 hrs</div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1">Offline Kitchen Survivability</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Security Sections -->
      <div class="space-y-10 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">01.</span>
            Fail-Closed Database & Multi-Tenant Isolation
          </h2>
          <p>
            In mission-critical healthcare operations, silent data loss during network interruptions is unacceptable. Shoreline Care OS employs an explicit <strong>fail-closed</strong> architecture:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Elimination of Split-Brain Fallback</strong>: When configured with PostgreSQL in production, Shoreline never silently falls back to a temporary local SQLite store on connection failure. Requests halt cleanly with transactional rollbacks, preserving database integrity.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Tenant Facility Scoping</strong>: Every database table containing clinical or operational data includes a mandatory <code>facility_id</code> foreign key indexed and verified by middleware on every query.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Private HTTP Cache Invalidation</strong>: Intermediate proxies are prohibited from caching Protected Health Information. All clinical endpoints emit <code>Cache-Control: private, no-cache, must-revalidate</code> tagged with the tenant facility ID.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">02.</span>
            Cryptographic Standards & Key Derivation
          </h2>
          <p>
            Shoreline applies modern cryptographic primitives at every layer of the technology stack:
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-3 text-xs">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">Argon2id Authentication</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                Passwords are hashed using memory-hard Argon2id (m=65536, t=3, p=4) with per-user cryptographic salts. Resistant against GPU-accelerated dictionary and rainbow table attacks.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">AES-256-GCM Encryption</div>
              <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                All persistent database volumes, automated snapshot backups, and stored EDI credentials are encrypted at-rest using AES-256 in Galois/Counter Mode.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            Network transmissions enforce <strong>TLS 1.3</strong> exclusively, protected by automated HSTS headers (HTTP Strict Transport Security with 1-year max-age and preload directives), Content Security Policy (CSP), and Helmet HTTP protection.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">03.</span>
            Immutable Audit Logging & Chain of Custody
          </h2>
          <p>
            In adherence to CMS-2567 dietary regulations and HIPAA audit rules, Shoreline maintains an append-only audit ledger (<code>audit_log</code> table):
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Non-Repudiation</strong>: Every resident diet order modification, IDDSI texture downgrade, NPO order, and Registered Dietitian EHR triage resolution records the verified actor user ID, previous value, proposed value, and timestamp.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Database Immutability Triggers</strong>: PostgreSQL triggers prevent <code>UPDATE</code> or <code>DELETE</code> operations against historical audit log rows.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>HACCP Corrective Action Enforcement</strong>: When food or refrigerator temperatures fall outside safe thresholds (&lt;140°F hot hold, &gt;41°F cold hold, &lt;165°F cook temp), the entry cannot be closed without documented corrective actions.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">04.</span>
            Hardware & Kitchen Tablet Ergonomics
          </h2>
          <p>
            Kitchen kiosks operate under demanding physical conditions:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) Direct Connection</strong>: Food probe temperatures are collected directly via standard Web Bluetooth LE drivers, bypassing untrusted cloud intermediaries.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Offline Mutation Sync Queue</strong>: In the event of Wi-Fi interruptions in basement kitchens or walk-in coolers, meal dispatches and HACCP logs are buffered in IndexedDB and re-synchronized upon reconnection.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Touch Safety Targets</strong>: Mobile and kiosk buttons strictly adhere to &ge; 44px touch targets with high-contrast color indicators to prevent mis-taps during active service lines.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">05.</span>
            Cloud Service Level Agreement (SLA)
          </h2>
          <p>
            Shoreline guarantees <strong>99.9% monthly availability</strong> for our managed SaaS multi-tenant API. Availability is defined as successful responses (HTTP &lt; 500) to client requests originating from verified facility networks.
          </p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto my-3">
            <table class="w-full text-xs text-left border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800/60 font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-2.5">Monthly Uptime Percentage</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5">Service Credit %</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-2.5">&ge; 99.9%</td>
                  <td class="p-2.5">Target SLA Achieved</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-2.5">99.0% – 99.89%</td>
                  <td class="p-2.5">10% of monthly subscription fee</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-2.5">95.0% – 98.99%</td>
                  <td class="p-2.5">25% of monthly subscription fee</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-2.5">&lt; 95.0%</td>
                  <td class="p-2.5">50% of monthly subscription fee</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">06.</span>
            Vulnerability Disclosure & Security Inquiries
          </h2>
          <p>
            We welcome responsible security disclosures from healthcare researchers and white-hat security professionals. To report a security concern or request our completed SOC 2 questionnaire:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono space-y-1 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            <div>Shoreline Operations LLC — Information Security</div>
            <div>Attn: Chief Information Security Officer (CISO)</div>
            <div>412 Commercial Street, Suite 400</div>
            <div>Portland, ME 04101</div>
            <div>PGP Key ID: 0x4D10B992</div>
            <div>Email: security@shorelineops.com</div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Action Navigation -->
      <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-between items-center text-xs">
        <a href="/terms" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline font-semibold">
          <span>Review Terms of Service</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
        <a href="/privacy" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-900 dark:hover:text-white">
          <span>Read Healthcare Privacy Policy & BAA</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
